Z||000007||fiero56||08-12-2001||11:49 PM||||I would like to meet Hulki sometime. Sitting at a table listening about all the crap he had to deal with just to get the Fiero to production. All the conflicts with design, options, drive-train, decalls, etc. <P>Ed is by far my Favorite current Fiero guru. That man knows more about these cars than anyone I have ever met. I still remember sitting at dinner with 87ECO5 Ed and Rosie this spring. That was awsome.||||reg||1
Z||000008||MooCow||08-13-2001||12:26 PM||||I too would have to vote for Ed Parks.  He does know what he is talking about and is very nice.<BR>Also have to give props to Cliff for this wonderful forum, Archie for his V8's, and also Aus for his body mods.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||10
Z||000009||Raydar||08-13-2001||12:43 PM||||Ed Parks.<BR>Cliff.<BR>Archie.<BR>Rodney.<BR>Fiero Store.<BR>I could keep going...<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000010||Leadfoot||08-13-2001||12:56 PM||||I'd have to say<P>Cliff - without him I'd have no one to talk to about fieros.  (Thanks man!)<P>Paul Vargyas - saw his v-8 formula a couple of years ago while I was driving home which has inspired me to buy a fiero of my own.  (Thank you for showing me the way!)  <P>Archie - helped me get some parts that I need for my fiero really bad, not to mention the kick a$$ body kits he has for sale.  Also, IMO he is the founding father for the v-8 fiero.  (Thanks for the help and for making the v-8 kits....you rock!)<P>Rodney Dickman - the man to go to when you need odd ball parts like the transmission selector bushings or a factory subwoofer.  (Keep up the great work and product line!) <P>Mr. Mike's - the sultan of leather seat covers.  (Thank you for saving my a$$....literally!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>The forum members - such as Oreif, Pondski, Fleabitdog.....and everyone else (yes, even EdsB52) for enlightening me on the inner workings of the fiero, selling me fiero goods, and just being there to shoot the Sh!t.  (Thanks...group hug....girls only please.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Haze_Performance||08-13-2001||01:28 PM||||In no particular order:<P>-Cliff Pennock<P>-Paul Vargyas<P>-V8 Archie <P>-The Fiero Shop<P>-The Fiero Store<P>-Rodney Dickman <P>-Mr. Mike's <P>-Chris Pond (Pondski)<P>-fierodave (Dave)<P>-Ausfiero (Jim)<P>-Toms Fiero Accessories<P>-Twin Lakes Fiero (Bob)<P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">         <BR></A><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="green"><B>Hello, My name is Haze. I'm the jerk that sits behind you at a traffic light & rattles your <BR>fillings loose with the unnecessarily loud stereo system.</B></FONT></FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000012||Alex4mula||08-13-2001||01:54 PM||||1. I have my 88 Formula since new. There was a time between 1992-1995 that finding parts for 88s wasn't easy (at least for me). If the Fiero Store (& their excellent customer service) would not exist I probably would not have my Fiero today.<BR>2.  There was also a guy called Matt Gruber (or similar) that had a very nice newsletter in late 80s/early 90s. Don't know what happened to him. That one helped me a lot also on mods and fixes by that time.<BR>3. Archi for being able to at least dream for more than 10 yrs about a V8 Fiero<BR>4. Ed Parks for my 3.4 & his factory<BR>5. All clubs and fans that thru the years took the time to write articles on mods & fixes.||||reg||1
