Z||000018||ChadMan||08-14-2001||09:41 AM||||FOCOA is far from perfect, but Phil and Gloria Huff have made a greater and more lasting contribution to the Fiero community at large than anyone else I can think of.  We *****  every year about the venue, the hotel, and the judging at the Nationals, but without Phil and Gloria we'd have no Nationals to *****  about at all.<P>And then there's Ed Parks.  I nominate him for Fiero sainthood.  He's always willing to help out a Fiero nut in trouble...too kind for his own good sometimes.  And he knows more about Fieros than anyone I've ever met.  A walking P-car encyclopedia.<P>Can't overlook Archie either.  I know he's ruffled a feather or two, but his V8 Fieros certainly lend respectability to the community as a whole.<P>You might not know Ot Huster, but I wouldn't have a Fiero today if it weren't for him.  I was looking to sell my '84 and buy something else when I saw Ot and his '84 at an all-Pontiac show.  He told me about FOCOA and the local clubs and got me excited about Fieros again.  (He won the show, too.)<P>Last and certainly not least: Cliff Pennock.  The man who brought all of us together.<P>Nice of you to mention us, Scott - though I haven't done much for the Fiero community except post smartass comments on the Forum and lose a lot of street races.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000019||MinnGreenGT||08-14-2001||10:25 AM||||On a much smaller/regional note.  I would have to nominate Pete Grosz (current MFF president) -he started the Minnesota Fiero Club many years ago, and has always acted in the best interest of the club itself. Initially doing everything himself, from the newsletter to event organization and more. He has always done everything possible to enlighten Fiero owners and spread the joy of the Fiero.<P>I also would like to recognize the Fiero Fanatics themselves, Tom & John (sorry I'm not even going to guess the spelling of their last name) from Wisconsin.  I first met them years ago at the national meet in Michigan.  They have some of the craziest ideas, but always follow through to bring us great creative Fieros and awsome events (Dells Run 2001   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>And I think that all activist Fiero owners should be thanked for sharing their love of the car!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg">   <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 08-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Haze_Performance||08-14-2001||04:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B>In no particular order:<P>-Cliff Pennock<P>-Paul Vargyas<P>-V8 Archie <P>-The Fiero Shop<P>-The Fiero Store<P>-Rodney Dickman <P>-Mr. Mike's <P>-Chris Pond (Pondski)<P>-fierodave (Dave)<P>-Ausfiero (Jim)<P>-Toms Fiero Accessories<P>-Twin Lakes Fiero (Bob)<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I forgot to add Oreif.. How did I forget the Doortab God?? (Also. without his help.. I would have NEVER gotten off my lazy a$$ and changed my engine mounts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) <P>Please forgive me Mr. Doortab.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">         <BR></A><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="green"><B>Hello, My name is Haze. I'm the jerk that sits behind you at a traffic light & rattles your <BR>fillings loose with the unnecessarily loud stereo system.</B></FONT></FONT>||||reg||11
